title: c2c send prints false no-relay-connector-detected warning when a bare c2c relay connect is running (only managed daemons detected)
updated_at: "2026-07-14T06:18:51Z"
---
Symptom: `c2c send <alias>@<host>` prints

  warning: queued locally; no relay connector detected — run `c2c relay connect` ...

even when a relay connector IS running and messages are actually being delivered. The warning is self-contradictory: it tells you to run the very command that is already running.

Repro:
1. Start the connector as a bare foreground process: `c2c relay connect` (e.g. in tmux, or backgrounded by a harness) — NOT via `c2c managed start relay-connect`.
2. `c2c send peer@host "msg"`.
Result: the "no relay connector detected" warning prints on every remote send, while `c2c whoami` simultaneously reports `connector: live (last sync Ns ago)` and the message does deliver (the peer replies).

Root cause: ocaml/cli/c2c_send_cmd.ml, `relay_connector_running_best_effort ()` (~line 138) only detects a *managed* relay-connect daemon, via `C2c_health_cmd.read_managed_instances` filtered on `mi_client = "relay-connect" && mi_status = "running"`. A bare `c2c relay connect` has no managed-instance dir / outer.pid, so it is invisible to the probe. The code comment acknowledges this and argues the fallback warning is "still accurate (we have no evidence one is running)" — but in practice it is misleading: it causes users/agents to believe delivery failed and take wrong actions (re-run connect, switch to `c2c relay dm send`, or report a false send failure).

The authoritative signal already exists: `c2c whoami` reports connector liveness from broker-owned relay sync state (`registered_live — connector bridge live ... last sync 12s ago`). The send-time probe simply does not use it.

Suggested fix: make `relay_connector_running_best_effort ()` also return true when either
  (a) the broker-owned relay connector sync-state is fresh — the same source whoami/health already use (e.g. last sync within a small window); or
  (b) a foreground `c2c relay connect` is detectable via a pidfile/lock that the connect command writes (or a process scan).
Prefer (a): reuse the existing fresh-sync signal so managed and foreground connectors are treated identically, then suppress/downgrade the warning whenever a live connector is detected.

Impact: correctness of delivery reporting (follow-on to B088). Non-breaking — delivery works — but actively confusing and causes wasted/incorrect agent actions. Observed live 2026-07-13 with a bare `c2c relay connect` (whoami: connector live, last sync 12s) while every `c2c send @host` printed the false warning.